The rest of this post may have some spoilers:

What I learned:
1) Famine is instantly deadly if you eat him.
2) Cancellation is the best wand to use against the wizard.
3) Ao Magical Breathing would have made water level quicker.
4) Levitation would have made Air level easier.
5) Check you inventory before you ascend!!! (activate all your
figurines, drink all you healing potions, polymorph all your imitation
amulets) 
6) Don't try to convert altars in the Astral plane! It is rather
annoying when you have to wait for 50 stupid monsters to finish their
moves with every step you take.

The end-game was rather simple, My life was only in danger when the
wizard reappeared. I could have wiped out the entire top level if I
wasn't tired of playing.
I should have tried praying in Hell. It would have been amusing to see
Moloch try to punish me. I killed both his priests before converting
the altars and that was a laugh.

No special highlights in the main dungeon. 
	I fond a few magic  lamps, and obtained Excaliber early on. 
	I found every lawful non-quest weapon, except Trollsbane. I
also made Orcrist and Sting, found Cleaver, and Grimtooth. Eventually
I made a little room, and dropped every weapon except Excaliber. So
much for the seven artifact limit.  I really wanted Grayswandir.
	I found only two wands of polymorph (one was in the end-game,
and I forgot to use it) This is very annoying considering all the
useless wands I found on the Samurai's quest. The polypiling got me a
lot of gems, and some nice tools, but nothing that I was looking for.
	Wand of wishing was wasted once trying for Grayswandir, and
only gave me one blessed sroll of charging, then packed away until the
endgame (where I used it for gold detection scrolls and dusted it for
a wand of polymorph)
	There was a 5 month hiatus in the middle of my game which
caused a lot of problems with me forgetting where my various stashes
were.
	I the entire game I only got 2 AoLS before the endgame. and
only two death wands. I found that the cancellation wand was much
better against the Wizard, since it negated his powers _every_ time,
while the Death wands were always missing him. (I had one time where I
shot at him and it bounced between me and a wal four times, never
hitting him)

